-- title:
--   Idelic norm-coset index equals the idele class Tate number
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a Galois extension of $K$, and let $D$ be a datum of type `IdeleGaloisDescent (𝓞 L) K L`, that is, a monoid homomorphism $\tau \mapsto D.\mathrm{act}\,\tau$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K) = (L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L)$ to the ring automorphisms of the adele ring $\mathbb{A}_L$, each continuous and each satisfying $D.\mathrm{act}\,\tau\,(\iota_L x) = \iota_L(\tau x)$ for $x \in L$, where $\iota_L$ is the structural map $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$. Let $\beta : \mathbb{A}_K \to \mathbb{A}_L$ be a ring homomorphism, $\mathrm{Nrm} : \mathbb{A}_L^{\times} \to \mathbb{A}_K^{\times}$ a monoid homomorphism, and $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ an element such that every $\tau$ lies in the subgroup of integral powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic with generator $\sigma$). Assume: $\beta(\iota_K x) = \iota_L(x)$ for $x \in K$; $\beta$ is injective; a unit $u \in \mathbb{A}_L^{\times}$ is fixed by $D.\mathrm{unitsAct}\,\tau$ for all $\tau$ exactly when $u$ lies in the image of $\beta$ on units; for every $u$ with $(D.\mathrm{unitsAct}\,\tau\,u)^{-1} u$ a principal idele for all $\tau$, $u$ lies in the subgroup generated by the image of $\beta$ on units together with the principal ideles $\iota_L(L^{\times})$; and $\prod_{\tau} D.\mathrm{unitsAct}\,\tau\,u = \beta(\mathrm{Nrm}\,u)$ for all $u$. Then the index in $\mathbb{A}_K^{\times}$ of the subgroup generated by the principal ideles $\iota_K(K^{\times})$ and the range of $\mathrm{Nrm}$ equals the cardinality of the quotient of the kernel of $c \mapsto (\sigma \cdot c)c^{-1}$ on the idele class group $C_L = \mathbb{A}_L^{\times}/\iota_L(L^{\times})$ by the image there of $c \mapsto \prod_{\tau} \tau \cdot c$, the two maps being induced by $D$ on $C_L$.
--
--   This is the class-field-theory dictionary identifying the idelic norm-coset index $[\mathbb{A}_K^{\times} : \iota_K(K^{\times})\cdot \mathrm{Nrm}(\mathbb{A}_L^{\times})]$ with the cardinality of $\hat{H}^0(\mathrm{Gal}(L/K), C_L)$, here stated for abstract descent, base-change and norm data $(D,\beta,\mathrm{Nrm})$ bound by structural hypotheses rather than for the genuine base change. It is used in the computation of the Herbrand quotient of the idele class group in the cyclic case and in the divisibility statement for the Tate cardinality when the extension has prime degree.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_M4aHerbrand_idelicNormCoset_index_eq_ideleClassTateCard.lean

import Definitions.Def_M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab
import Mathlib.FieldTheory.Galois.Basic

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
